# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
dist/
*.egg-info/

# uv
# uv.lock is intentionally committed for reproducible installs

# DuckDB
data/
*.duckdb
*.duckdb.wal

# Node / TypeScript
ts/node_modules/
ts/dist/
ts/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
js/node_modules/

# Environment
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Editor
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Private — never committed. Named explicitly, not just the parent, so that removing or
# narrowing the _private/ line alone would not silently re-expose these paths — see
# phase-priv-04 and tools/check_no_private_content.py, which enforces this at commit time.
_private/
_private/portfolio/
_private/portfolio/projects/

# Working scratchpad — local only. Ephemeral task detail, briefs, audits and drafts live here
# and are never committed. Nothing in it is deleted without the owner's explicit approval
# (PLAN-015). .gitkeep predates this rule and stays tracked; one other file was tracked by
# explicit exception for a single completed phase to delete as its own last step, and was
# removed when that phase completed.
_working/
!_working/.gitkeep

# Agent worktrees — guard only; the sanctioned location is ../d-system-worktrees/
_worktrees/

# Capture — raw intake (_capture/raw), the inbox (_capture/inbox) and staging
# (_capture/staging). Private by default (ADR-007 section 8): only records a promotion
# step deliberately moves into _data/ are ever tracked. See PLAN-009 phase-cap-03.
_capture/

# Browser-verification output — screenshots dropped in the repository root by a phase's
# visual checks, and the Playwright MCP server's own working directory. Ignored for two
# reasons. They are regenerable: the finding a screenshot supported belongs in the session
# record as prose, and the image can be produced again by re-running the check. And they
# are unscannable: tools/check_no_private_content.py skips .png content by design
# (CONTENT_CHECK_SKIP_SUFFIXES), so a screenshot is the one tracked file the content gate
# cannot read — the eight that prompted this rule each showed the shell prompt, putting a
# username and hostname in frame with nothing able to catch it.
#
# Anchored to the root so it never touches a deliberate image inside docs/ or templates/.
# The tracked SVG diagrams under docs/07-architecture/diagrams/ are unaffected.
/*.png
.playwright-mcp/

# NOT ignored, deliberately: .agents/ and .codex/. They look like tool directories but are
# declared deliverables of the portable-agent-workflows phases — .agents/skills/*/SKILL.md
# and .codex/agents/*.toml are named in docs/09-backlog/backlog.yaml. Ignoring either would
# silently drop a peer's work. See PLAN-020.
